    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0322" n="248" xml:id="pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/740a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-24T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 24, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1864. For your information. In reply to an inquiry as to whether we would join
                    with the Allies in an agreement not to recognize independently any new Russian
                    Government, the Department has informed the French Ambassador that we would be
                    glad to exchange views with the Allies at any time on the subject but that we
                    would not bind ourselves to a course which might look to Russia as a measure of
                    compulsion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
